PKG=zz9ksvc46
NAME=zz9ksvc-k46 1.0.0-2 - ZZ9000-family service channel module, k46 line
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.0.0-2
CATEGORY=system
CLASSES=none zz9ksvc
VENDOR=amix
PSTAMP=amix-zz9ksvc46-1.0.0-2
# Kernel space (amix-dlm C2-2, C3-5 v4 sec 1): a role=module entry of the #ext kpkg block
# (line=k46), never an ordinary entry.  Catalog name zz9ksvc-k46, pkginst zz9ksvc46; VERSION
# is kernel/modules/zz9ksvc/module/VERSION, the same on both lines.  The nodes are in class
# zz9ksvc (C3-5 v18 sec 1.2).  Licence: GPL-3.0-or-later.
APKG_DESC=The service channel of a ZZ9000-family board's second ARM core (/dev/zz9ksvc0, 1: buffers and requests for the board's services runtime, every one checked by the kernel) as a demand-class kernel module for the 68040/68060 line module kernel kernel-k46-m: /etc/conf/mod.d/zz9ksvc and its nodes.  GPL-3.0-or-later.
DESC=The kernel/modules zz9ksvc driver built as an amix-dlm kernel module for the 68040/68060 line: demand class, loaded at the first open of /dev/zz9ksvc0 or 1 and kept only while a board with a runtime is there (it takes the board from zz9kbus, which it names in depend); character major 55, its nodes /dev/zz9ksvc0 and 1 (c 55 0, c 55 1, 0666) shipped by the package.  Per-open buffers by handle, mmap by handle cookie, bounded waits, quarantine of buffers a timed-out request uses.  Page zz9ksvc(7).  /etc/conf/modreg.d/zz9ksvc holds the package's defaults (none).  The package writes no boot store; after the install apkg runs kbootset build and commit (or prints the command when bootset=manual).  GPL-3.0-or-later.
